# UI Sizing Adjustments

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Reduce "Up Next" Hero Size
In [frontend/app/page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/page.tsx):
* Decrease padding from `p-6` to `p-4` or `p-5`.
* Decrease `min-h-[180px]` to `min-h-[120px]` or `min-h-[140px]`.
* Decrease title font size from `text-3xl` to `text-2xl`.
* Decrease action buttons padding and maybe switch `mt-5` to `mt-3`.
* This will create a more compact header that takes up less vertical space.

### 2. Fix AI Chat Extending (Scrolling)
In [frontend/app/page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/page.tsx):
* The primary content wrapper currently has `overflow-y-auto`, which allows the entire bottom half of the dashboard to scroll infinitely as the chat grows.
* Change the wrapper's classes to `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto lg:overflow-hidden pr-1`. This allows scrolling on mobile but strictly bounds the height on desktop.
* Ensure the right sidebar column also has `overflow-y-auto` (it already does for `custom-scrollbar`).
* This will force the [CommandCenter](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/dashboard/CommandCenter.tsx#47-110) to fit the remaining window height on desktop and enable its internal scrolling for the chat. 

